    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN a <description>, and it is INSIDE the root
        element on purpose - a comment ABOVE <StandardValueSet> breaks `sf` deploy at
        conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml file".

        PHASE 2 (2026-08-14) RETIRED 'PSA', REPLACING IT WITH 'Under Contract (PSA)'.
        'Under Contract (PSA)' sits immediately after where 'PSA' used to be listed so that
        removing 'PSA' left the pipeline order intact (LOI -> Under Contract (PSA) ->
        About to Close). <sorted> is false, so position here is the displayed order.

        <forecastCategory>Forecast</forecastCategory> and <probability>85</probability> on
        'Under Contract (PSA)' were COPIED FROM THE RETIRED 'PSA' ENTRY VERBATIM, not chosen.
        They are the whole reason this was a value migration rather than a new stage:
        forecastCategory drives every forecast roll-up and probability drives Expected
        Revenue, so a deal that moved from 'PSA' to 'Under Contract (PSA)' did not move in
        any forecast.

        NO %2F ENCODING APPLIES TO 'Under Contract (PSA)'. It contains spaces and
        parentheses but no slash. The 'Dead/Pass' entry below is LITERAL here and is
        encoded 'Dead%2FPass' only inside BusinessProcess/RecordType metadata; that
        precedent invites exactly the wrong instinct. Do not encode the parentheses.

        'PSA' IS NOW FULLY RETIRED (Phase A2 reconciliation, 2026-08-17). This file
        previously carried a 'PSA' <standardValue> with <isActive>false</isActive>, described
        at the time as "P2-D3, staged, not applied here" - that description was stale: the
        org's live StageName picklist had already dropped 'PSA' entirely (not even present as
        an inactive value), confirmed via a live sobject describe of Opportunity against
        usman-dpeg. That local/org drift is reconciled here by deleting the block outright
        rather than deploying it as inactive. Every other Opportunity-stage metadata file that
        once referenced the bare 'PSA' literal (business processes, validation rules, the
        Deal_Bucket__c formula, path assistants) was already repointed to 'Under Contract
        (PSA)' during Phase 2 - re-verified by repo-wide grep on 2026-08-17, no remaining
        active reference to bare 'PSA' exists outside this historical note. The
        agent-output/p2-d3-retire-psa/ directory this comment used to point to no longer
        exists in this repo (confirmed 2026-08-17).
    -->
